olded, followed by nested sub-bullets listing the exclusion cases and a brief generalization note explaining that the key is the semantic role of the head noun rather than any specific symptom word or predicate verb. I want to make sure the span stays unified—including adjectival premodifiers like \"abnormal\"—to match how the gold annotation treats the whole phrase as one DiseaseClass mention rather than splitting out a separate modifier tag.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Generic Manifestation or Pathological State as DiseaseClass:** IF a noun phrase's head denotes a generic clinical manifestation (a sign, symptom, or structural/developmental abnormality) or a generic pathological state (such as a deficiency or dysfunction of a biomolecule expressed through a prepositional complement), with no disease-type head noun and no proper-name disease label, AND the phrase is the complement of a predicate that characterizes a disease or causally links it to a disease-governed subject (e.g., \"is characterized by,\" \"results in,\" \"is caused by\"), THEN tag the full noun phrase, including its premodifiers and prepositional complement, as one DiseaseClass span rather than O.\n  - **Does NOT apply when:** (a) the span is a named disease or uses a disease-type head noun (e.g., a \"[X] disease/syndrome/disorder/cancer\" construction, or a named \"[X] deficiency\"), which is SpecificDisease; (b) the span is only a gene, protein, or molecule name with no pathological qualifier, which is O; (c) the predicate frame is present but the complement is not a manifestation or pathological state (e.g., a treatment, a population, or a neutral anatomical site), because the frame alone does not license the label; (d) the span is a coordinated list of disease terms functioning as a single composite mention, which is CompositeMention.\n  - **Basis for recognition:** Decide from the semantic role of the head noun (manifestation or state versus named entity), not from any specific symptom word, and not from the predicate verb alone.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1890, "output_tokens": 2835, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2318}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}